7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\nWrong attempts used: 0/8. Demo requests used: 1/8.\nReply with exactly one action JSON on the last line.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    g = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    h, w = len(g), len(g[0])\n    points = sorted((r, c) for r in range(h) for c in range(w) if g[r][c] == 2)\n    start, end = points[0], points[-1]\n\n    holes = []\n    for r in range(h):\n        cols = [c for c in range(1, w - 1)\n                if g[r][c - 1] == g[r][c] == g[r][c + 1]\n                and g[r][c] not in (g[0][0], 2)]\n        # Select the middle cell of each horizontal three-cell opening.\n        for c in cols:\n            if g[r][c - 2 if c >= 2 else c] != g[r][c] or c == 1:\n                if c + 2 < w and g[r][c + 2] != g[r][c]:\n                    holes.append((r, c))\n    holes.sort()\n\n    path = [start]\n    current = start\n    for r, c in holes:\n        path.append((r - 1, current[1]))\n        path.append((r - 1, c))\n        path.append((r, c))\n        current = (r, c)\n    path.append((end[0], current[1]))\n    path.append(end)\n\n    for (r1, c1), (r2, c2) in zip(path, path[1:]):\n        if r1 == r2:\n            for c in range(min(c1, c2), max(c1, c2) + 1):\n                g[r1][c] = 2\n        else:\n            for r in range(min(r1, r2), max(r1, r2) + 1):\n                g[r][c1] = 2\n    return g\n```\n\n{\"action\": \"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit","correct":false,"valid":true}},{"step":54,"kind":"observation","phase":"act","t0":1794142873.017,"t1":1794142887.667,"alias":"task-d439bccd","message":"Feedback since your last action:\nYour submission was INCORRECT. Wrong attempts so far: 1.\n\nSame instance. Task id: task-d439bccd\nTest input (30x30):\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 2 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 